WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.283
A price rises 20 percent,

2
00:00:02.283 --> 00:00:04.250
then falls 20 percent.

3
00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:05.432
Is it back where it

4
00:00:05.432 --> 00:00:07.162
started? No.

5
00:00:07.508 --> 00:00:09.232
Start at 100.

6
00:00:09.232 --> 00:00:12.359
Up 20 percent makes 120.

7
00:00:12.359 --> 00:00:15.122
Down 20 percent of 120

8
00:00:15.122 --> 00:00:16.041
is 24.

9
00:00:16.041 --> 00:00:18.144
That leaves 96.

10
00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:20.019
Add the two changes,

11
00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:22.288
plus their product over 100.

12
00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:23.742
20 minus 20,

13
00:00:23.742 --> 00:00:24.721
minus 4.

14
00:00:24.721 --> 00:00:26.033
A net fall of 4

15
00:00:26.033 --> 00:00:27.188
percent.

16
00:00:27.886 --> 00:00:30.081
Percent change and percentage points

17
00:00:30.081 --> 00:00:31.255
are different.

18
00:00:31.255 --> 00:00:32.816
A rate going from 4

19
00:00:32.816 --> 00:00:34.377
to 5 percent is one

20
00:00:34.377 --> 00:00:36.319
point, but a 25 percent

21
00:00:36.319 --> 00:00:37.271
rise.

22
00:00:37.601 --> 00:00:38.872
Your turn.

23
00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:40.863
What's the net change?
